 "notes": "The south-eastern corner of Small Giftun (Giftun Seghir): the fringing reef, the plateau at 15-25 m where the day boats moor, the shelf running north from its north-east corner along the vertical east wall (past 100 m), and the usual drift south along the wall onto the plateau. The zones and drift come from dive-centre descriptions (redseacreatures.com), so extents are approximate. Erg Somaya is left off. The origin is on the mooring area; the site's stored coordinates are the island's centre, about 1.5 km north-west.",
